--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Behavioral port attribution (LangChain / LangGraph / Deep Agents / LangSmith)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The CoreAgentGraph, CoreAgentDeep, CoreAgentEngine, CoreAgentSkills, and
CoreAgentTalon modules are an independent Swift re-implementation of runtime
*concepts and behaviors* popularized by the following LangChain, Inc. projects.
No source code was copied from them; only observable behavior, public API
semantics, and documented design contracts informed the Swift implementation:

  LangGraph            - durable super-step graph runtime, checkpoints,
                         pending writes, interrupts/resume, time travel,
                         Send fan-out, parent command routing, subgraphs,
                         deferred nodes.
                         https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph

  Deep Agents          - task-ledger / planning harness, virtual filesystem,
                         sub-agent orchestration, human-in-the-loop review,
                         rubric middleware, RLM orchestration.
                         https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents

  LangChain            - agent/middleware composition patterns.
                         https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain

  LangSmith (Engine)   - run tracing, evidence/receipt ingestion, and the
                         closed-loop issue/feedback scanner that CoreAgentEngine
                         models.
                         https://www.langchain.com/langsmith

LangGraph, Deep Agents, and LangChain are open-source and licensed by LangChain,
Inc. under the MIT License. LangSmith is a proprietary hosted product of
LangChain, Inc. (only its client SDK, langsmith-sdk, is MIT-licensed); no
LangSmith source or service is used here — CoreAgentEngine independently models
observable closed-loop behaviors it popularized. Their names and trademarks
belong to their respective owners and are used here only to describe the origin
of the ported behaviors, not to imply endorsement.

CoreAgent keeps Apple's Foundation Models types (Prompt, Transcript, Tool,
GeneratedContent, Generable, LanguageModelSession) as the native primitives; the
ported concepts are adapted to that contract rather than reproducing the Python
message/model abstractions.

